(4422380, 626038, 49804, '<td valign="top">Very creative idea, and i like having the focus on the lego man, the lighting is a bit too harsh here though, maybe trying to light from the side. Adding some softer lighting would help a lot here, also adding a solid background of white or black would add a lot to the shot, very creative though.</td>', 'Very creative idea, and i like having the focus on the lego man, the lighting is a bit too harsh here though, maybe trying to light from the side. Adding some softer lighting would help a lot here, also adding a solid background of white or black would add a lot to the shot, very creative though.', '2008-01-24 18:09:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4485992, 625703, 90263, '<td valign="top">LOL thats funny!</td>', 'LOL thats funny!', '2008-02-14 08:45:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4528014, 625584, 76430, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your PB.  I''m still trying to figure out the guy in the background.  It looks like a burglar, but I''m guessing it''s someone either opening presents or rushing to work?  I can definitely identify with this.  I lost my work cell phone while taking pictures in tidepools, and was HOPING it didn''t get replaced with a Crackberry.  Alas it did, the same model as yours.</td>', 'Congratulations on your PB.  I''m still trying to figure out the guy in the background.  It looks like a burglar, but I''m guessing it''s someone either opening presents or rushing to work?  I can definitely identify with this.  I lost my work cell phone while taking pictures in tidepools, and was HOPING it didn''t get replaced with a Crackberry.  Alas it did, the same model as yours.', '2008-02-29 13:08:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4576470, 625503, 80904, '<td valign="top">When I see this shot, it cracks me up all the time. Great work there. I bet it took some courage to dress up like that lol</td>', 'When I see this shot, it cracks me up all the time. Great work there. I bet it took some courage to dress up like that lol', '2008-03-20 10:37:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605545, 625656, 53964, '<td valign="top">Hmm, I thought I''d left a comment on this before...<br/> <br/>Your expression made me laugh, and your lighting is good on your face (or whoever''s face it is). Overall, it''s definitely not a bad picture, but may I offer a few comments (nitpicks) that might help next time? :) (Keep in mind I don''t know any more than you, it''s just things that caught my eye.)<br/> <br/>Yes, the background... even if you can''t change it moving the seating away from it so it can blur would help :)<br/> <br/>The shirt... plain and darker would probably work better... more contrast for your face and no distraction of logo :)<br/> <br/>Since it was advanced editing (and presuming you have the software) it may have helped to burn the lettering on the book a bit, to make it jump out more. As is, the shirt logo caught my eye first when I looked to see what was causing the expression, then moved on to the swear box :)<br/> <br/>Hands held a little higher so they didn''t need to be cropped, and would be in front of the smoother shoulder area of the shirt (in other words, think about their "backdrop" too) :)<br/> <br/>You could have gotten even pickier and cloned out the seam in the couch, too.<br/> <br/>One of the biggest things I''ve learned here (though still forget to implement) is attention to detail. Believe me, there''s always someone out there who will notice that speck of fuzz or stray hair or SOMEthing, no matter how carefully you think you''ve looked! lol<br/> <br/>Hope you don''t mind me picking apart your shot, but it''s because I think it''s worth it :)</td>', 'Hmm, I thought I''d left a comment on this before... Your expression made me laugh, and your lighting is good on your face (or whoever''s face it is). Overall, it''s definitely not a bad picture, but may I offer a few comments (nitpicks) that might help next time? :) (Keep in mind I don''t know any more than you, it''s just things that caught my eye.) Yes, the background... even if you can''t change it moving the seating away from it so it can blur would help :) The shirt... plain and darker would probably work better... more contrast for your face and no distraction of logo :) Since it was advanced editing (and presuming you have the software) it may have helped to burn the lettering on the book a bit, to make it jump out more. As is, the shirt logo caught my eye first when I looked to see what was causing the expression, then moved on to the swear box :) Hands held a little higher so they didn''t need to be cropped, and would be in front of the smoother shoulder area of the shirt (in other words, think about their "backdrop" too) :) You could have gotten even pickier and cloned out the seam in the couch, too. One of the biggest things I''ve learned here (though still forget to implement) is attention to detail. Believe me, there''s always someone out there who will notice that speck of fuzz or stray hair or SOMEthing, no matter how carefully you think you''ve looked! lol Hope you don''t mind me picking apart your shot, but it''s because I think it''s worth it :)', '2008-04-02 06:00:30.000000', NULL, 0),
